# Technical details: {{ this_model }}

The [model card](./README.md) answers which size to use and how this set compares with other quantizations of [{{ base_model }}](https://huggingface.co/{{ base_model }}). This page has what is behind those numbers: what each eval slice is, every slice compared on its own, how the composite is built, and how to reproduce the quantizations.

All numbers are **excess KLD**: how far a quant's next-token distribution is from the unquantized model's, minus the unquantized model's own rounding noise (the *noise floor*, measured by perturbing the unquantized model's activations at bf16 precision). Lower is better; 0 would be indistinguishable from the original. Where two quants both sit within about twice the noise floor, their difference is within the original's own noise and is marked as such.

