# The composite

{% if weight_spec %}The composite weights real user prompts {{ '{0:0.2f}'.format(weights.wild) }} and real agent sessions {{ '{0:0.2f}'.format(weights.swe) }}: {{ weight_spec.notes }}{% else %}The composite weights real user prompts {{ '{0:0.2f}'.format(weights.wild) }} and real agent sessions {{ '{0:0.2f}'.format(weights.swe) }}, the default for a general-purpose model.{% endif %}

Two uses, computed differently:
- *Which size* (the card's first table): the weighted sum of the two slices' excess KLD, the expected per-token damage for a usage mix with that share of tokens.
- *Against other quants* (the card's second table and plot): the weighted geometric mean of the per-slice ratios. A sum of excesses lets the slice with the larger absolute excess dominate whatever its weight (real user prompts' excess runs several times agent sessions'); the geometric mean gives each slice its stated weight. A slice where both quants sit within about twice its noise floor is left out of the comparison and the other reweighted.

