# Calibration

{% if calibration.calibration %}Calibration: **{{ calibration.calibration }}**{% if calibration.generator %}, its answers generated by an {{ calibration.generator }}{% endif %}.{% if calibration.shares %} Rows by slice: {% for k, v in calibration.shares.items() %}{{ k }} {{ '{0:0.2f}'.format(v) }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% if calibration.doc_kinds %}; English document kinds {{ calibration.doc_kinds }}{% endif %}{% if calibration.cal_rows %}; {{ calibration.cal_rows }} rows of {{ calibration.cal_cols }} tokens{% endif %}.{% endif %}

The calibration covers what models read and write at work rather than only web text: documents pasted into user turns and returned as tool results (prose, code, and real commits as diffs in 30 languages and formats), short tool-use loops, a little of the model's own voice, and the default corpus. How each part was chosen and measured is in [docs/calibration.md](https://github.com/yeasah/vllm-exl3-plugin/blob/main/docs/calibration.md).
